      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] The description transcribes code expressions verbatim and includes local absolute paths in the `TEST\u003d` tags.\n\n1. **Diff Narration:** Avoid restating the exact `while` loop condition from the code in the description. A brief conceptual explanation is better.\n2. **Local Paths in TEST tags:** The `TEST\u003d` tags contain local developer mount paths (`/mnt/.../chromiumos/...`) which will not be meaningful to other developers or in the git history. Consider shortening these to just the commands run (e.g., `cros format --check board/coral/board.c`).\n\n**Suggested replacement:**\n```text\ncoral: Reload watchdog in board_tcpc_init battery wait loop\n\nDuring board initialization, coral waits up to 2 seconds for a\ndisconnected battery to wake up.\n\nSince board_tcpc_init() runs as a HOOK_INIT hook, periodic tick\nhooks (which normally handle watchdog reloads) have not yet started.\nIf a DUT has a dead, uninitialized, or slow-waking battery, the\nwait loop can exceed the ~1.127 s hardware watchdog timeout on\nNPCX5, causing the EC to reset and loop indefinitely.\n\nReload the watchdog explicitly in each iteration of the battery\nwait loop to avoid tripping the watchdog during early HOOK_INIT\nexecution.\n\nBUG\u003dNone\nTEST\u003dmake BOARD\u003dcoral\nTEST\u003dcros format --check board/coral/board.c\nTEST\u003dcros lint board/coral/board.c\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/567ed3e5-994b-4e01-a45e-8f9680b95c0f)",
